# ==========================================================================
# The repository holds only the program, a short README and the results.
# Everything else in this folder (manuscript drafts, logbook, ISEF forms,
# literature notes, handoffs, PDFs, Word files, slides) stays on this machine.
# A new file at the top level is ignored unless it is whitelisted here.
# ==========================================================================
/*
!/.gitignore
!/README.md
!/config.py
!/requirements.txt
!/holoparasitic/
!/scripts/
!/tests/
!/data/
!/figures/
!/empirical/
!/hydraulics/

# hydraulics/: only the measured Kleaf table, which run_kleaf_validate.py and
# run_resistance_convention_sensitivity.py read. The rest of the Matos deposit
# (including UCBG_venation_form_data/, ~4.4 GB) is downloaded from Dryad,
# doi:10.5061/dryad.1g1jwsv36. Note that the venation data also sits in git
# history (commits e667fe7..76febe6); ignoring it does not rewrite that history.
/hydraulics/*
!/hydraulics/hydraulics/
/hydraulics/hydraulics/*
!/hydraulics/hydraulics/UCBG_venation_kmax.csv

# Documents are never tracked, even inside the kept folders
*.md
!/README.md
*.pdf
*.doc
*.docx
*.xlsx
*.pptx
*.tex
*.html
~$*

# ==========================================================================
# Scripts that build the paper, appendices, logbook, forms, slides or the
# display board rather than computing results
